## Try it in a browser / Kokeile selaimessa

```bash
python app.py
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8000. The page takes this solution's inputs, starts
`run_poc.py` and shows the result, the output files and the run's log. Each run works
in a temporary folder of its own; `sample_input/` and `output/` here are not written
to. A run without an added file uses the examples in `sample_input/`.
The page also shows the solution's steps and hands out its source code as a zip.

Käynnistä `python app.py` ja avaa http://127.0.0.1:8000. Sivu ottaa vastaan ratkaisun
syötteet, ajaa `run_poc.py`:n ja näyttää tuloksen, tulostiedostot ja ajon lokin.
Sivu näyttää myös ratkaisun vaiheet, ja siltä saa lähdekoodin zip-tiedostona.

The page has no sign-in and listens on this computer only. It needs nothing beyond
`requirements.txt`; `python app.py --port 8080` picks another port.
Its font is Sora, under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (`ui/fonts/OFL.txt`).

Another front end (a Next.js app, for one) can call the same server from its own
server side:

- `GET /api/solution`: what the solution is, its inputs and its output fields (`ui/solution.json`).
- `POST /api/run`: a multipart form with `files` and, where the solution takes them, `question` or `text`; answers `{ok, exit_code, log_tail, outputs: [{name, kind, size, url}], result}`.
- `GET /api/source`: this package's source code as a zip, the page's "Download source code" / "Lataa lähdekoodi". It holds the package's Python files (`app.py` among them), `README.md`, `config.yaml`, `requirements.txt`, `.env.example` (left out if it gives a key a value) and `.gitignore`, the text files in `schemas/` and `prompts/`, and the page's own files in `ui/`, and nothing else: no other hidden file (so never `.env`), no file whose name says it holds a credential (`credentials.json`, `secrets.toml`, `id_rsa`), nothing from `sample_input/`, `output/` or `evals/ground_truth/` (in any case of their names), and no virtual environment. It is off while the page listens on the network (`--host`).

